\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. King of glory, King  of peace,
\par I will love Thee;\b 
\par \b0 And that love may never cease,
\par I will move Thee.
\par Thou hast granted my request
\par Thou hast heard me
\par Thou didst note my working breast
\par Thou hast spared me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Wherefore with my utmost art
\par I will sing Thee
\par And the cream of all my heart
\par I will bring  Thee
\par Though my sins against me cried,
\par Thou didst clear me
\par And alone when they replied,
\par Thou didst hear me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Seven whole days not one in seven,
\par I will praise Thee
\par In my heart, though not in heaven,
\par I can raise Thee
\par Small it is, in this poor sort
\par To enroll Thee
\par E'en eternity's too short
\par To extol Thee.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs16 
\par }

